Like Level teleport traps, polymorph traps disappear after the
character steps on it, so the warrior's trap detection scheme (finding
traps by stepping on them) doesn't really work.  You could very well
have stepped on a polymorph trap.  In fact, I would bet money on it.
The only way I know of to prevent this from happening is to detect the
traps before you step on them.  Rings of searching and wands of secret
door detection are useful to that end.  It has been my experience that
sometimes, when a character returns to human form, he loses the dragon
scale armor, while other times he doesn't.  I am not entirely sure
what affect the probability of retaining the armor, but I think the
blessed/cursed status is important.  There are two ways of returning
to human form; going below 0 hp or simply waiting it out.  Going below
0 hp will force a return to human form, but you might be without armor
and will certainly not be wielding a weapon, and since this would
probably happen in a combat situation, 'twould be ill advised.  There
is no difference between a suit of dragon scale mail that is created
normally and one that is wished for, except the latter may be created
with plusses.  (Why wish for +0 gray d.s.m. when you can get it +3?)

